        {
          "id": 1919870,
          "username": "Lauren_Scott",
          "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/community.shopify.com/lauren_scott/{size}/417640_2.png",
          "created_at": "2026-10-22T06:37:48.475Z",
          "cooked": "<p>Most restock notification tools send to every subscriber for a variant when it comes back in stock, so the “first 8 only” behavior is the part to verify before you buy. Ask the vendor the exact question: does a restock send fire once per variant, and can the number of emails be limited to the quantity added? Get the answer in writing, since “support is great” doesn’t tell you whether it’s a setting or a custom build.</p>\n<p>If the answer is no, you have two practical options. The simple one is to turn off automatic restock emails, export the signup list with timestamps, and email the first N people yourself when you restock.</p>\n<p>The other option is a small custom app. Subscribe to the inventory level update webhook and compare each new quantity with the previous one. Only a positive change counts as a restock, because every sale also fires that webhook. When the delta is positive, email the oldest N signups and mark them as notified.</p>",
          "post_number": 3,
          "post_type": 1,
          "posts_count": 3,
          "updated_at": "2026-10-22T06:37:48.475Z",
