      "id": 1849163,
      "summarized_text": "The request is for a Shopify restock-notification app that limits alerts to the number of units added—for example, notifying only the first eight subscribers when eight items return to stock. A participant recommends Back In Stock Alert / Notify Me, which adds a signup button and automatically sends emails when inventory is replenished, but cannot confirm whether it supports quantity-based limits. Another advises verifying this exact behavior with the vendor, including whether alerts can be capped by the restock quantity, and getting confirmation in writing.\n\nIf the app does not offer this feature, two alternatives were suggested: disable automatic alerts and manually email the earliest signups after exporting the list, or build a custom app. The custom approach would track Shopify inventory-update webhooks, detect positive inventory changes, and notify the oldest subscribers up to the increase, while avoiding treating sales-related inventory decreases as restocks. No app capability or final solution has been confirmed, so the question remains open.",
